From: Husky WiFi Fix <husky-wifi-fix@local>
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] soc: google: add WLAN/BT runtime recovery watchdog

For intermittent failures (WiFi works when cold, dies when warm),
add a kernel watchdog that monitors for "PCI not powered on" and
"wifi driver unloaded" conditions, then triggers a controlled
WLAN/BT subsystem reset without full reboot.

This addresses the Android framework giving up after 10 WiFi restarts
(WifiSelfRecovery: Already restarted wifi 10 times... Disabling wifi).

Signed-off-by: Husky WiFi Fix <husky-wifi-fix@local>
---
 drivers/soc/google/wlan_bt_recovery.c | 210 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/soc/google/Kconfig            |   8 +
 drivers/soc/google/Makefile           |   1 +
 3 files changed, 219 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/google/Kconfig b/drivers/soc/google/Kconfig
index 0000000..5555555 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/google/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/google/Kconfig
@@ -1,3 +1,11 @@
+config WLAN_BT_RECOVERY
+	tristate "Pixel WLAN/BT runtime recovery watchdog"
+	depends on ARCH_ZUMA || ARCH_ZUMAPRO
+	default y
+	help
+	  Watchdog for Pixel 8 series WiFi/BT PCIe failures. Triggers
+	  subsystem reset when link drops. Helps thermal/intermittent cases.
+
